[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
Change the game speed in [b]coop[/b] (campaign and skirmish missions played in multiplayer). In vanilla the game speed is locked in every network game: with this mod the host presses [b]Backspace[/b] during the mission, picks a speed in the game's own [b]Game speed[/b] menu, and everyone in the match switches to it.

[b]Only the host[/b] (the player who creates the match) needs the mod. The other players need nothing: their games follow the host's speed through the game's own network protocol.

[size=4][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Download the zip from the Files tab.[/*]
[*]Extract it into the game folder, the one that contains [b]binaries[/b] and [b]mods[/b], e.g. [i]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Call to Arms - Gates of Hell[/i]. If Windows asks, overwrite [b]version.dll[/b]: it's the same file in all my mods. [b]If you use GOHSE[/b] (Gates of Hell Script Extender), don't overwrite it: keep GOHSE's version.dll, and the script the zip puts in [i]gohse/mods/goh_dll_mods[/i] loads the mod.[/*]
[*]Host a coop match, then press [b]Backspace[/b] during the mission.[/*]
[/list]After installing you should have:
[code]<game>\binaries\x64\version.dll
<game>\binaries\x64\goh_mods\coop_game_speed.dll
<game>\gohse\mods\goh_dll_mods\   (used only with GOHSE)[/code]No data mod and no change to the mod list: it's only the DLL, so it doesn't affect joining matches.
[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete [i]binaries\x64\goh_mods\coop_game_speed.dll[/i]. If you have none of my other mods installed, also delete [i]binaries\x64\version.dll[/i], the [i]goh_mods[/i] folder and [i]gohse\mods\goh_dll_mods[/i].

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The vanilla [b]Backspace[/b] Game speed menu works in coop, and the whole match follows the chosen speed.[/*]
[*]Speeds: 1 = x0.28, 2 = x0.56, 3 = x1 (normal), 4 = x2, 5 = x3 (the vanilla x3.3 is capped to x3).[/*]
[*]No desync: the 20 ms simulation step never changes, only the pacing of the steps that the server already sends to every player.[/*]
[*]In single player nothing changes: the game handles speed itself.[/*]
[*]The game files on disk are never modified: the DLL patches the game in memory only. If a game update changes the code it needs, it skips that part and the game runs unmodded.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Call to Arms - Gates of Hell: Ostfront, x64, tested on game versions [b]1.067.0[/b] and [b]1.069.0[/b].[/*]
[*]Works with or without [url=https://github.com/nature2468/gohse]GOHSE[/url], the Gates of Hell Script Extender (from the 1.0.2 version).[/*]
[*]No other mods needed. The mod loader ([b]version.dll[/b]) is included in the zip.[/*]
[/list][b]Notes[/b]
[list]
[*]While the Game speed menu is open the host's game is paused, so the other players may briefly see "waiting for server".[/*]
[*]Troubleshooting logs: [i]%TEMP%\goh_coop_game_speed_call_to_arms.exe.log[/i] and [i]%TEMP%\goh_coop_game_speed_call_to_arms_server.exe.log[/i][/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Source code[/b][/size]
Open source, built from a single C file. Source, build instructions and my other Gates of Hell mods (Coop Checkpoint, Loot Highlight, Inspect Preview): [url=https://github.com/nicko996/goh-coop-mods]github.com/nicko996/goh-coop-mods[/url]

